ren and i have to  know that we are alienated intellectual  i mean that broadly speaking this is  what we are we are alienated  intellectuals and so we [ __ ] about the  government and we critique the monetary  system and so forth and so on  well then you see your children on the  brink of the reason and you say you know  geez my alienation has brought me  alienation but i can't let the kids grow  up to be marked to be pawns of the  market economy and the propaganda  machine people scratching their heads  trying to figure out whether they're  Republicans or Democrats I can't put  that on my children and so then you say  well okay then they must join in the  alienation they must be taken out of the  culture as we were taken out of the  culture and this is a momentous decision  because you this act of separating from  the culture is unambiguously alienating  and yet it seems to be the only way to  find the self  otherwise you never contact the self you  contact a commodified cartoon of the  self that finds meaning and outboard  motors and basketball  and you know all this other crap that's  peddled as reality so our relationship  to our culture I think is a very  uncomfortable one and of course  psychedelics exacerbate this and you  know I think if you have children that  it's one thing to talk a lien nation but  once they get to the place where they're  asking to take LSD or to take Phyllis  Hyman and you know Kafka said a  wonderful thing I think it's in the  penal colony he said you can choose to  be freed but it's the last choice you'll  ever and that's that's sort of the  dilemma in which we find ourselves  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

